Subject: [PATCH] WebRTC: include a track identifier for initially muted senders

A send transceiver created without a track still needs the track-id part
of its SDP MSID, including when the stream-id is "-". Generate an initial
identifier for the muted source; replacing its track can then publish
media using an already identified sender.

--- a/Source/WebCore/Modules/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaEndpoint.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/Modules/mediastream/gstreamer/GStreamerMediaEndpoint.cpp
@@ -1669,10 +1669,14 @@
         msidBuilder.append(source->mediaStreamID());
         if (auto track = source->track())
             msidBuilder.append(' ', track->id());
+        else
+            msidBuilder.append(' ', createVersion4UUIDString());
     }, [&](Ref<RealtimeOutgoingVideoSourceGStreamer>& source) {
         msidBuilder.append(source->mediaStreamID());
         if (auto track = source->track())
             msidBuilder.append(' ', track->id());
+        else
+            msidBuilder.append(' ', createVersion4UUIDString());
     }, [](std::nullptr_t&) { });

     int payloadType = pickAvailablePayloadType();
